nergy-association-articles-1942">Articles</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-custom menu-item-object-custom menu-item-27426"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/webinars/" class="ammonia-energy-association-webinars-27426">Webinars</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-custom menu-item-object-custom menu-item-7425"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/events/" class="ammonia-energy-association-conferences-7425">Conferences</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-custom menu-item-object-custom menu-item-3439"><a href="/presentations/" class="ammonia-energy-association-presentations-3439">Presentations</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-has-children menu-item-3477" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/members/" class="ammonia-energy-association-membership-3477">Membership</a><ul class="sub-menu"><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-28411"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/members/register-industry-member/" class="ammonia-energy-association-register-as-an-industry-member-28411">Register as an Industry Member</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-28410"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/membership-directory/" class="ammonia-energy-association-aea-membership-directory-28410">AEA Membership Directory</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-28361"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/sign-up-for-our-newsletter/" class="ammonia-energy-association-sign-up-for-our-newsletter-28361">Sign up for our Newsletter</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-custom menu-item-object-custom menu-item-32410"><a href="https://portal.ammoniaenergy.org/" class="ammonia-energy-association-member-login-32410">Member Login</a></li></ul></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-has-children menu-item-3932" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/about/" class="ammonia-energy-association-about-3932">About</a><ul class="sub-menu"><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-29740"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/about/leadership/" class="ammonia-energy-association-aea-leadership-29740">AEA Leadership</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-28359"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/about/aea-employees/" class="ammonia-energy-association-aea-staff-28359">AEA Staff</a></li></ul></li></ul></div><nav class="search_indicator"><a href="" class="headersearch icon--search" data-expand=".search_container"> <span class="sink_icon sink_svg"> <svg id="search-icon" data-name="icon-search" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 55 55"><title>Search</title> <path d="M58.58,43.77A14.85,14.85,0,0,0,43.77,29,14.85,14.85,0,0,0,29,43.77,14.85,14.85,0,0,0,43.77,58.58,14.85,14.85,0,0,0,58.58,43.77ZM75.5,71.27a4.3,4.3,0,0,1-4.23,4.23,3.94,3.94,0,0,1-3-1.26L57,62.94A23.21,23.21,0,0,1,34.73,65.2a23.18,23.18,0,0,1-7.44-5,23.59,23.59,0,0,1-5-7.44,23.24,23.24,0,0,1,0-18.08,22.8,22.8,0,0,1,12.4-12.4,23.24,23.24,0,0,1,18.08,0,23.59,23.59,0,0,1,7.44,5,23.18,23.18,0,0,1,5,7.44A23.21,23.21,0,0,1,62.94,57L74.28,68.29A4.08,4.08,0,0,1,75.5,71.27Z" transform="translate(-20.5 -20.5)"/> </svg> </span> </a></nav></nav><nav class="socialmedia menu_horizontal" role="social_media"><ul></ul></nav></div></header><main  class="onepage" id="maincontent" role="main"><section class="content"><header class="pageinfo archiveinfo"><div class="centering_box"><h1><span class="archive_metalabel">Site items in: </span><span class="archive_title">Ammonia Energy Import/Export</span></h1></div></header><div class="flexible archives-filter"><div class="centering_box archive-inner"><article class="odd_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost1 archivepost_first flexible pt-articles post-34358 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-economic-implementation category-market-development regions-europe regions-north-america regions-united-states topics-ammonia-bunker-fuel topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-markets topics-ammonia-production topics-ccs-ammonia topics-infrastructure topics-maritime-fuel"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/cf-industries-trafigura-and-tfg-marine-to-facilitate-adoption-of-marine-ammonia-fuel/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to CF Industries, Trafigura and TFG Marine to facilitate adoption of marine ammonia fuel"><picture> <source type="image/webp" data-lazy-srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/cf-donaldsonville-wide-aerial-640x359.jpg.webp"/> <img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="CF Industries, Trafigura and TFG Marine to facilitate adoption of marine ammonia fuel" data-lazy-src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/cf-donaldsonville-wide-aerial-640x359.jpg"/><noscript><img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/cf-donaldsonville-wide-aerial-640x359.jpg" alt="CF Industries, Trafigura and TFG Marine to facilitate adoption of marine ammonia fuel"/></noscript> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34358"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/cf-industries-trafigura-and-tfg-marine-to-facilitate-adoption-of-marine-ammonia-fuel/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to CF Industries, Trafigura and TFG Marine to facilitate adoption of marine ammonia fuel">CF Industries, Trafigura and TFG Marine to facilitate adoption of marine ammonia fuel</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/julianatchison/'>Julian Atchison</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> January 23, 2026 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> The trio plan to build on a series of already successful collaborations between CF Industries and Trafigura, and push forward bunkering logistics planning for marine ammonia fuel on the US Gulf Coast and northwest Europe.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/cf-industries-trafigura-and-tfg-marine-to-facilitate-adoption-of-marine-ammonia-fuel/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="even_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost2 flexible pt-articles post-34300 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-economic-implementation category-international-trade category-market-development regions-asia regions-japan regions-north-america regions-united-states topics-ammonia-demand topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-markets topics-ammonia-production topics-ammonia-storage topics-ammonia-transportation topics-ammonia-coal-dual-fuel topics-ccs topics-ccs-ammonia topics-certification topics-infrastructure topics-power-generation"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/jera-outlines-full-supply-route-to-bring-low-carbon-ammonia-from-usa-to-japan/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to JERA outlines full supply route to bring low-carbon ammonia from USA to Japan"><picture> <source type="image/webp" data-lazy-srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/JERA-Hekinan-modifications-640x360.png.webp"/> <img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="JERA outlines full supply route to bring low-carbon ammonia from USA to Japan" data-lazy-src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/JERA-Hekinan-modifications-640x360.png"/><noscript><img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/JERA-Hekinan-modifications-640x360.png" alt="JERA outlines full supply route to bring low-carbon ammonia from USA to Japan"/></noscript> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34300"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/jera-outlines-full-supply-route-to-bring-low-carbon-ammonia-from-usa-to-japan/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to JERA outlines full supply route to bring low-carbon ammonia from USA to Japan">JERA outlines full supply route to bring low-carbon ammonia from USA to Japan</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/julianatchison/'>Julian Atchison</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> January 19, 2026 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> Time-charter contracts covering a total of four vessels have been signed with NYK Bulkship and Mitsui O.S.K. Lines to transport ammonia from Louisiana to JERA’s Hekinan Thermal Power Station in Hekinan City, Japan.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/jera-outlines-full-supply-route-to-bring-low-carbon-ammonia-from-usa-to-japan/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="odd_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost3 flexible pt-articles post-34268 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-economic-implementation category-international-trade category-market-development regions-asia regions-europe regions-india topics-ammonia-demand topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-markets topics-ammonia-production topics-ammonia-transportation topics-certification topics-mega-project topics-renewable-ammonia"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/uniper-am-green-sign-long-term-offtake-for-renewable-ammonia-from-india-to-europe/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Uniper, AM Green sign long-term offtake for renewable ammonia from India to Europe"><picture> <source type="image/webp" data-lazy-srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/uniper-am-green-combined-logos-640x172.png.webp"/> <img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Uniper, AM Green sign long-term offtake for renewable ammonia from India to Europe" data-lazy-src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/uniper-am-green-combined-logos-640x172.png"/><noscript><img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/uniper-am-green-combined-logos-640x172.png" alt="Uniper, AM Green sign long-term offtake for renewable ammonia from India to Europe"/></noscript> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34268"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/uniper-am-green-sign-long-term-offtake-for-renewable-ammonia-from-india-to-europe/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Uniper, AM Green sign long-term offtake for renewable ammonia from India to Europe">Uniper, AM Green sign long-term offtake for renewable ammonia from India to Europe</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/julianatchison/'>Julian Atchison</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> January 13, 2026 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> The long-term, binding offtake agreement has been signed for renewable ammonia produced at AM Green’s under-development facility in Kakinada, India. 500,000 tons per year of RFNBO-certified ammonia will be shipped to Europe as early as 2028. The agreement has been in the works since 2023.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/uniper-am-green-sign-long-term-offtake-for-renewable-ammonia-from-india-to-europe/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="even_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost4 flexible pt-articles post-34262 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-economic-implementation category-international-trade category-market-development regions-europe regions-germany regions-netherlands topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-markets topics-ammonia-storage topics-ammonia-transportation topics-cracking-ammonia topics-infrastructure"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/lbc-duisport-development-of-new-ammonia-terminal-in-the-ruhr-industrial-region/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to LBC & duisport: development of new ammonia terminal in the Ruhr industrial region"><picture> <source type="image/webp" data-lazy-srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Duisport_LBC-640x334.jpg.webp"/> <img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="LBC &amp; duisport: development of new ammonia terminal in the Ruhr industrial region" data-lazy-src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Duisport_LBC-640x334.jpg"/><noscript><img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Duisport_LBC-640x334.jpg" alt="LBC &amp; duisport: development of new ammonia terminal in the Ruhr industrial region"/></noscript> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34262"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/lbc-duisport-development-of-new-ammonia-terminal-in-the-ruhr-industrial-region/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to LBC &#038; duisport: development of new ammonia terminal in the Ruhr industrial region">LBC & duisport: development of new ammonia terminal in the Ruhr industrial region</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/geofrey-njovu/'>Geofrey Njovu</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> January 13, 2026 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> LBC Tank Terminals and duisport will jointly develop an inland ammonia terminal in Duisburg, connecting the key industrial hub to an under-development ammonia import, storage and cracking terminal in Vlissingen, the Netherlands.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/lbc-duisport-development-of-new-ammonia-terminal-in-the-ruhr-industrial-region/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="odd_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost5 flexible pt-articles post-34258 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-financing category-government-initiative category-international-trade category-market-development regions-africa regions-namibia topics-ammonia-demand topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-markets topics-finance topics-funding-opportunities topics-mega-project"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/namibia-new-funding-for-renewable-ammonia-production/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Namibia: new funding for renewable ammonia production"><img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Namibia: new funding for renewable ammonia production" data-lazy-src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Flag_of_Namibia-640x427.png" /><noscript><img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Flag_of_Namibia-640x427.png" alt="Namibia: new funding for renewable ammonia production" /></noscript></a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34258"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/namibia-new-funding-for-renewable-ammonia-production/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Namibia: new funding for renewable ammonia production">Namibia: new funding for renewable ammonia production</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/geofrey-njovu/'>Geofrey Njovu</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> January 13, 2026 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> Two Namibia-based renewable ammonia projects – Hyphen Hydrogen Energy and Zhero Molecules Walvis Bay – have received development funding from the African Development Bank and the SDG Namibia One Fund, respectively.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/namibia-new-funding-for-renewable-ammonia-production/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="even_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost6 flexible pt-articles post-34223 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-economic-implementation category-financing category-government-initiative category-international-trade category-market-development regions-asia regions-japan topics-ammonia-combustion topics-ammonia-demand topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-production topics-ammonia-storage topics-ammonia-transportation topics-ammonia-coal-dual-fuel topics-ccs topics-ccs-ammonia topics-cement-decarbonization topics-energy-carrier topics-infrastructure topics-mega-project topics-power-generation"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/from-louisiana-to-japan-new-government-support-to-establish-full-supply-chains-by-2030/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to From Louisiana to Japan: new government support to establish full supply chains by 2030"><picture> <source type="image/webp" srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/20251219_PressJERAs-Initiatives-for-Establishing-the-Low-Carbon-Ammonia-Value-Chain-Concept-Diagram-640x168.png.webp"/> <img data-no-lazy="" fetchpriority="high" src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/20251219_PressJERAs-Initiatives-for-Establishing-the-Low-Carbon-Ammonia-Value-Chain-Concept-Diagram-640x168.png" alt="From Louisiana to Japan: new government support to establish full supply chains by 2030"/> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34223"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/from-louisiana-to-japan-new-government-support-to-establish-full-supply-chains-by-2030/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to From Louisiana to Japan: new government support to establish full supply chains by 2030">From Louisiana to Japan: new government support to establish full supply chains by 2030</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/julianatchison/'>Julian Atchison</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> December 21, 2025 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> Mitsui & Co. and JERA announced that they have been awarded CfD funds by the Japanese government to support the import of CCS-based ammonia from the Blue Point project in Louisiana, USA. By 2030 (2029 in JERA’s case), full supply chains will be established to import the ammonia into Japan, for use in the power generation, cement manufacturing, and other industrial sectors.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/from-louisiana-to-japan-new-government-support-to-establish-full-supply-chains-by-2030/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="odd_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost7 flexible pt-articles post-34213 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-economic-implementation category-government-initiative regions-europe topics-ammonia-demand topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-markets topics-ammonia-production topics-ammonia-storage topics-biogas-ammonia topics-biomass-ammonia topics-ccs-ammonia topics-electrolysis topics-emissions topics-energy-security topics-feedstock-comparisons topics-finance topics-infrastructure topics-life-cycle-analysis topics-low-carbon-fertilizers topics-policy topics-regulations topics-renewable-ammonia"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/technology-choices-to-meet-the-eus-new-climate-targets-for-2040/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Technology choices to meet the EU’s new climate targets for 2040"><picture> <source type="image/webp" srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/eu-flag-640x427.png.webp"/> <img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/eu-flag-640x427.png" alt="Technology choices to meet the EU’s new climate targets for 2040"/> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34213"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/technology-choices-to-meet-the-eus-new-climate-targets-for-2040/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Technology choices to meet the EU’s new climate targets for 2040">Technology choices to meet the EU’s new climate targets for 2040</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/kevin-rouwenhorst/'>Kevin Rouwenhorst</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> December 18, 2025 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> The EU has set a legally binding climate target for 2040, at a 90% GHG emission reduction versus 1990 levels. But, while the 2030 emission target can theoretically be met with limited modifications to existing ammonia production plants in the EU, new technology pathway choices will have to be made well before 2040 to ensure compliance. We explore some of the options, and projects in progress.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/technology-choices-to-meet-the-eus-new-climate-targets-for-2040/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="even_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost8 flexible pt-articles post-34173 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-annual-review category-commercial-technologies category-conference category-demonstration-project category-economic-implementation category-financing category-government-initiative category-international-trade category-market-development category-research-development regions-global topics-ammonia-bunker-fuel topics-ammonia-combustion topics-ammonia-demand topics-ammonia-energy-conference topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-engine topics-ammonia-gas-turbine topics-ammonia-markets topics-ammonia-production topics-safety topics-ammonia-storage topics-ammonia-transportation topics-ammonia-coal-dual-fuel topics-catalysts topics-ccs topics-ccs-ammonia topics-ccs-hydrogen topics-ccus topics-cement-decarbonization topics-certification topics-cracking-ammonia topics-distributed-ammonia-synthesis topics-dual-fuel topics-electrolysis topics-emissions topics-emissions-testing topics-energy-carrier topics-feedstock-comparisons topics-finance topics-fuel-cells topics-fuel-comparisons topics-funding-opportunities topics-houston-2025 topics-infrastructure topics-insights topics-life-cycle-analysis topics-low-carbon-fertilizers topics-maritime-engine topics-maritime-fuel topics-mega-project topics-nox-emissions topics-perth-2025 topics-pipeline-transport topics-policy topics-power-generation topics-public-perception topics-regulations topics-renewable-ammonia topics-renewable-hydrogen topics-solar-ammonia topics-transportation-fuel topics-zero-carbon-shipping"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/2025-an-ammonia-energy-rollercoaster/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to 2025: an ammonia energy rollercoaster"><picture> <source type="image/webp" data-lazy-srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/air-liquide-antwerp-cracker-startup-640x262.png.webp"/> <img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="2025: an ammonia energy rollercoaster" data-lazy-src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/air-liquide-antwerp-cracker-startup-640x262.png"/><noscript><img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/air-liquide-antwerp-cracker-startup-640x262.png" alt="2025: an ammonia energy rollercoaster"/></noscript> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34173"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/2025-an-ammonia-energy-rollercoaster/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to 2025: an ammonia energy rollercoaster">2025: an ammonia energy rollercoaster</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/julianatchison/'>Julian Atchison</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> December 17, 2025 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> Despite the successes and progress made in 2025, the year remains a missed opportunity for ammonia energy. The first complete supply chains for renewable ammonia are emerging, and some 600,000 tons of annual production capacity is set to be online in northeast China early next year. Maritime engines, cracking, and power & heat technology solutions also made their mark, moving from feasibility into deployment. But disappointing outcomes at the IMO and government support that failed to spark market development remains an issue, with plenty of critical, detail-heavy work ahead of us in 2026.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/2025-an-ammonia-energy-rollercoaster/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="odd_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost9 flexible pt-webinars post-34199 webinars type-webinars status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry regions-global topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-certification topics-emissions topics-emissions-testing topics-life-cycle-analysis"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/webinars/unpacking-the-aeas-ammonia-certification-system/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Unpacking the AEA’s Ammonia Certification System"><picture> <source type="image/webp" data-lazy-srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/AEA-Unpack-Amm-Cert-640x360.png.webp"/> <img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Unpacking the AEA’s Ammonia Certification System" data-lazy-src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/AEA-Unpack-Amm-Cert-640x360.png"/><noscript><img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/AEA-Unpack-Amm-Cert-640x360.png" alt="Unpacking the AEA’s Ammonia Certification System"/></noscript> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Webinar</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34199"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/webinars/unpacking-the-aeas-ammonia-certification-system/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Unpacking the AEA’s Ammonia Certification System">Unpacking the AEA’s Ammonia Certification System</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/julianatchison/'>Julian Atchison</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> Join us to explore the AEA’s now-operational Certification System. AEA Certification Project Manager Madhav Acharya will be joined in conversation by Nick Cook (CF Industries), and Vibeke Rasmussen (Yara Clean Ammonia).</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/webinars/unpacking-the-aeas-ammonia-certification-system/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><article class="even_post archive_post thumb_exists archivepost10 archivepost_last flexible pt-articles post-34178 articles type-articles status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry category-economic-implementation category-international-trade category-market-development regions-europe regions-middle-east regions-north-america regions-saudi-arabia regions-united-states topics-ammonia-demand topics-ammonia-energy-export topics-ammonia-markets topics-ammonia-production topics-ammonia-transportation topics-certification topics-infrastructure topics-mega-project"><div class="featimg"> <a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/air-products-yara-partner-to-advance-low-emissions-ammonia/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Air Products & Yara partner to advance low-emissions ammonia"><picture> <source type="image/webp" data-lazy-srcset="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/air-products-yara-640x360.png.webp"/> <img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Air Products &amp; Yara partner to advance low-emissions ammonia" data-lazy-src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/air-products-yara-640x360.png"/><noscript><img src="https://ammoniaenergy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/air-products-yara-640x360.png" alt="Air Products &amp; Yara partner to advance low-emissions ammonia"/></noscript> </picture> </a></div><div class="mainpost"> <span class="art-type">Article</span><header class="postinfo"><h2 id="post-34178"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/air-products-yara-partner-to-advance-low-emissions-ammonia/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Air Products &#038; Yara partner to advance low-emissions ammonia">Air Products & Yara partner to advance low-emissions ammonia</a></h2></header><div class="entry-meta"> <span class='authors-list'><a class='art-author' href='https://ammoniaenergy.org/author/julianatchison/'>Julian Atchison</a></span> <span class="entry-date"> December 15, 2025 </span></div><div class="text"><p class="excerpt"> The pair are in advanced negotiations to cement a partnership that will de-risk and progress two key production projects: the Louisiana Clean Energy Complex in the USA, and NEOM in Saudi Arabia.</p><aside class="readmore fancyfont"> <a class="button" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/articles/air-products-yara-partner-to-advance-low-emissions-ammonia/">Continue Reading</a></aside></div></div></article><nav class="archive_relatedposts relatedposts"><ul><li class="backward prev"></li><li class="forward next"><a href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/topics/ammonia-energy-export/page/2/" >More Items &raquo;</a></li></ul></nav></div></div></section></main><footer data-wpr-lazyrender="1" id="footer" role="contentinfo"><div class="footer-inner-container container-top"><div class="footer_inner centering_box"><div class="flexible"><div class="col"><div class="footerlogo"> <a class="logoclick dont_highlight" href="https://ammoniaenergy.org/"> <span class="sink_img sink_svg"> <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 472.07 80.15"><defs><style>.a{fill:#3c3;fill-rule:evenodd;}.b{fill:#010101;}.c{fill:#231f20;}</style></defs><title>Ammonia-Energy-Association-Logo-Horizontal-Color</title><path class="a" d="M13.16,68,39.39,52.88a7.39,7.39,0,0,1-.16-1.49,7,7,0,0,1,5.27-6.76V14.15a7,7,0,0,1-4.37-3.49L24.22,38.21l-16.17,28h.44A6.91,6.91,0,0,1,13.16,68Z"/><path class="a" d="M8.49,68.76a4.42,4.42,0,1,1-4.42,4.42,4.42,4.42,0,0,1,4.42-4.42Z"/><path class="a" d="M84.48,68.76a4.42,4.42,0,1,1-4.42,4.42,4.42,4.42,0,0,1,4.42-4.42Z"/><path class="a" d="M46.3,3a4.42,4.42,0,1,1-4.42,4.42A4.42,4.42,0,0,1,46.3,3Z"/><path class="a" d="M53,52.77,79.67,68.15a6.91,6.91,0,0,1,4.81-1.93h.07l-16.17-28L52.47,10.66a7,7,0,0,1-4.37,3.49V44.68A7,7,0,0,1,53,52.77Z"/><path class="a" d="M41,56.07A7,7,0,0,0,51.42,56L77.79,71.22a7,7,0,0,0-.28,2,6.92,6.92,0,0,0,.82,3.27H14.64A6.94,6.94,0,0,0,15.12,71Z"/><path class="b" d="M126.57,31.79H117.2l-1.89,4.69h-6l10-24.8h5.24l9.78,24.8h-5.95ZM125,27.41,122,19.08l-3.08,8.33Z"/><path class="b" d="M137.88,36.48l4-24.8h